course: dictionary
lesson: 12971
title: Exertion: hard work and effort
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exertion is a noun, and it means hard effort. It can be hard physical effort, like running or lifting, or hard mental effort, like thinking very hard about a tricky puzzle. «After the race, Sam was red-faced with exertion.» Sam's red face shows that he worked very hard.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Lifting the heavy box took great exertion.» The word great and the heavy box tell you that exertion means a lot of strength or work. When you read exertion, ask: what did someone have to do, and was it hard?
explain: Exertion is about using your strength or power. In PE, your heart beats faster after exertion, you breathe hard, and you sweat. Your body is working hard, so it is showing you the exertion.
fact: Exertion means hard physical or mental effort.
fact: Exertion also means using strength or power to do something.
fact: «Red-faced with exertion» means someone's face is red because they worked very hard.
fact: After exertion, your heart beats faster, you breathe hard, and you sweat.
fact: In science, exerting a force means pushing or pulling.
exercise: «After the race, Sam was red-faced with exertion.» What does exertion mean here? | *Hard effort that made him tired and hot | A prize for winning | A cold drink after a race | A loud cheer from the crowd
exercise: Your heart beats faster after exertion. What is exertion in that sentence? | *Hard physical effort, like running or climbing | Sleeping in bed | Eating a big lunch | Being still and resting
exercise: Find and copy the word that means hard effort: «Lifting the heavy box took great exertion.» | lifting | heavy | *exertion | box
test: «Pushing the heavy door shut needed a lot of exertion.» What does exertion mean? | *Using strength to push or pull | Opening a window to let air in | Painting the door a new colour | A quiet noise from the room
test: In science, what does exerting a force mean? | Reading a book quietly | Sleeping soundly | Singing a loud song | *Pushing or pulling
exam: Tom panted from the exertion of running up the stairs. What does exertion mean? | A happy song | A soft bed | A cold, damp breeze | *Hard effort using strength
